      "side": 1,
      "message": "This file is generated from MODULE.bazel (similar to how yarn.lock is generated from package.json) and *must not be modified manually*. Any manual changes to this file will be overwritten the next time `MODULE.bazel` is updated (for example, when adding a new `bazel_dep` or bumping a version for existing `bazel_dep`).\n\nSince the option you are looking for was flipped in the latest BCR release of `rules_python`, it should be sufficient to bump the version and explicitly depend on `rules_python` from BCR see: [1] in `MODULE.bazel`, for example:\n\n```python\nbazel_dep(name \u003d \"rules_python\", version \u003d \"1.8.0-rc1\")\n```\n\nAfter applying this change, running any Bazel command will automatically update `MODULE.bazel.lock`.\n\nAny update to `MODULE.bazel` should be accompanied by the corresponding update to the generated `MODULE.bazel.lock` file in the same commit, to avoid inconsistencies between declared and resolved dependencies.\n\nWith `bazel mod explain \u003cbzlmod\u003e` one can verify which version is used:\n\nYou can verify which version is being used with:\n\n```bash\n$\u003e bazel mod explain rules_python\n```\n\nExample output:\n\n```bash\n├───rules_python@1.8.0-rc1\n```\n\n[1]: https://registry.bazel.build/modules/rules_python/1.8.0-rc1",
      "revId": "abe5316239f48b3c58d0c680cb368e5f01680e77",
